WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.767
Local and private AI shift responsibility toward the organization.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:08.657
Teams may gain control over data flow, model selection, and runtime behavior,

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:11.916
but they also own more of the infrastructure.

00:00:11.916 --> 00:00:16.399
GPUs, CPUs, memory, storage, model caches, vector stores, backups, networking, queues,

00:00:16.399 --> 00:00:21.696
scheduling, monitoring, patching, and recovery planning all become part of the operating model.

00:00:21.696 --> 00:00:24.548
Cost drivers can be easy to underestimate.

00:00:24.548 --> 00:00:29.030
Accelerator time, idle resources, storage for model files, embeddings, logs, backups,

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.697
data movement, monitoring systems, and staff time all matter.

00:00:32.697 --> 00:00:38.809
A private system that appears inexpensive during a pilot can become expensive when many users,

00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:43.291
large context windows, multiple models, and retained telemetry enter the picture.

00:00:43.291 --> 00:00:46.958
Reliability matters because useful AI systems attract real work.

00:00:46.958 --> 00:00:52.255
Once people depend on the platform, downtime, slow responses, missing indexes, stale documents,

00:00:52.255 --> 00:00:55.515
failed backups, and unclear ownership become business problems.

00:00:55.515 --> 00:00:59.997
Resource limits, usage tracking, cleanup routines, model cache management, queue controls,

00:00:59.997 --> 00:01:04.072
and shutdown policies help prevent uncontrolled growth and surprise costs.

00:01:04.072 --> 00:01:08.961
A sovereign AI environment should include backup and restore plans, configuration management,

00:01:08.961 --> 00:01:11.813
capacity planning, incident ownership, and recovery procedures.

00:01:11.813 --> 00:01:16.296
It should also define what happens when a local node fails,

00:01:16.296 --> 00:01:19.963
a model endpoint is unavailable, an index is corrupted,

00:01:19.963 --> 00:01:22.407
or a cost threshold is exceeded.

00:01:22.407 --> 00:01:28.519
Infrastructure decisions should support the workflow without creating fragile operations that only one person understands.

00:01:28.519 --> 00:01:32.187
Operational planning should be tied to real usage patterns.

00:01:32.187 --> 00:01:37.484
Track which teams use which models, when demand spikes, which collections grow fastest,

00:01:37.484 --> 00:01:39.113
and where requests queue.

00:01:39.113 --> 00:01:43.188
That evidence supports right-sized hardware, cleanup work, and budget conversations.

00:01:43.188 --> 00:01:49.300
Sovereignty is easier to sustain when cost and reliability are visible before they become surprises.
